  "limitations": [
    "This changes argument forwarding and strict input validation; it does not establish native VINTF compatibility or claim the pinned main checker consumes the shipping API in a particular check.",
    "The native PropertyFetcher represents unsigned64-bit values. Canonical positive decimal validation is an intentional strict subset of native ParseUint syntax, not a list of valid released Android API levels.",
    "The unchanged property reader does not import first_api_level overrides and silently takes the last direct duplicate assignment. This patch does not change that parser.",
    "Only an absent GetProp result(None) permits fallback; present empty, malformed, noncanonical, conflicting or overflowing values fail.",
    "Current metadata/recovery/mi_ext/source compositions still pin the original wrapper. A new explicit composition must admit0011 before native adoption; all older contracts and receipts remain unchanged."
  ]
